From: COLDMANYU <46128522+COLDMANYU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] auron: fix LZ4_HADOOP framing interop with Hadoop/parquet-java

- writer: emit one block per 256 KiB chunk. Hadoop Lz4Decompressor (parquet-java)
  decompresses into a 256 KiB buffer, a single larger block fails with
  "LZ4Exception: Error decoding offset" (same bug as apache/arrow#49641 in C++).
- reader: follow Hadoop BlockCompressorStream: a block is one original-size header
  followed by as many (compressed size, chunk) pairs as needed to reach it. parquet-java
  writes pages larger than the codec buffer (e.g. big dictionary pages) that way; the old
  reader assumed one chunk per header. The block list may end with an empty (size 0)
  header that BlockCompressorStream.finish() writes after a large write.
---
